<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indo-Pakistani War of 1965</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1965">1965</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Second Kashmir War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Indo-Pakistani War of 1965 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> from August to September 1965. It began with Operation <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a>, an attempt by Pakistan to infiltrate fighters into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jammu">Jammu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>, and widened into large tank battles in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> ceasefire ended the fighting, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent-declaration">Tashkent Declaration</a> of January 1966 restored the prewar positions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indo-pakistani-war-of-1965.jpg" alt="Indo-Pakistani War of 1965" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abhinayrathore at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1965_Indo-Pak_War_DestroyedShermanTank.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
